WEBVTT

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.880
She has already drawn her last breath.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.210
Hey, you!

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.390
There's a rope stretched across here, right?

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.990
Sorry, so I'm really not allowed then.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.000
Don't move!

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.730
The landmines haven't all been cleared yet!

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.400
Landmines?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.770
Come back stepping in the footprints from when you walked in.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:57.950
I don't know where they are.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:01.620
Hang on.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.270
All right, let's go.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:29.140
I can't, my legs won't move.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.150
Thanks a bunch.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:20.220
But I'll bet the landmines were a fib, and you just wanted to get your arms around a girl, huh?

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.040
Hey!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.450
Had you going, huh?

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.520
You fool.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.390
I'm Azusa Himemiya.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.500
Terumichi Madoka...

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:01.200
Well, it's just good that nothing happened.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.430
So, why did you come to Uruk, Azusa?

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.540
I heard rumors while I was traveling,

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.840
...that a lot of paranormal phenomena happen here.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.450
Like that people heard voices they shouldn't have been able to hear,

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:18.680
...and that time reversed itself, and even that someone saw a god!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.960
So that means now one more person has been drawn here by Dynamis.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:25.960
Dynamis?

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.930
That's what we're calling the paranormal phenomena that occur here.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.260
Dynamis...

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.040
"Hidden power," in the Greek language.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:47.010
Why these sorts of phenomena occur, and what exactly lies dormant beneath these sands...

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.950
That's what we're investigating.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.020
That guy's a scientist too?

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.460
Yeah, and a brilliant one at that.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:55.720
Doesn't look it.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.560
This dig is going really smoothly since he came.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.770
In particular, his deciphering of inscriptions and his predictions based on those...

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.200
...about the distribution of the ruins are marvelous.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.200
All in spite of the fact that his specialty is astrophysics, so he's outside his field of expertise.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.340
I suppose you'd call a person like him a genius.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.490
That girl ended up staying on, huh?

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:29.590
They make a good couple, don't they?

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.720
Why does this area have all these tanks and landmines around?

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.890
There was a war at the beginning of this century.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.190
Even the cradle of civilization is in this state.

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:18.670
Something "-pota" civilization, wasn't it?

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:20.640
Mesopotamian civilization...

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.010
Uruk is also the homeland of the world's oldest story,

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.570
..."The Epic of Gilgamesh."

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.710
What's the "Whatsit of Gilgamesh"?

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:32.480
Gilgamesh is the name of a legendary king,

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.780
...who was said to be part god and part human.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.660
A tyrant whom the legend depicts as courageous and fierce, Gilgamesh.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.290
The people were made to suffer under his tyranny.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.790
But before him appeared a man named Enkidu.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:57.970
At first the two were foes, but through combat a friendship grew, and they became the best of friends.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:04.110
After encountering this companion, Gilgamesh transformed into a king who governed justly.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:11.590
But in due course, Enkidu incurred the wrath of the gods, and died.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:18.660
His companion's death provoked Gilgamesh to became obsessed with eternal life, and he departed on a journey.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:23.030
But he returned to his home having been unable to obtain it.

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:26.830
He started wanting eternal life just because his friend died?

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.630
What a weirdo, huh?

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:32.810
I'll bet maybe he had some kind of questionable relationship with that Enkidu guy or something.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:38.750
I don't know about that.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.290
En-ki-dou...

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.450
You're Enkidu!

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.090
It's true.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.960
Howard!

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.370
Terumichi found an underground ruin!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.430
What did you say?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.870
It's in ancient Sumerian!

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:38.970
I thought maybe I should play some music for it.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.140
Is this...

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.520
It appears it's not an ordinary cavern.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.850
Nothing shows up on the camera.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:57.630
What about the sensors?

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:00.030
No response from the laser range-finder.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:03.660
But that's... That device has a range of how many kilometers?

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:07.740
But I can't get a measurement, no matter what frequency of laser I use.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.230
Let's try shifting positions.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:14.570
No change.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.880
What about the others?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:18.440
The ultrasonic and microwave sensors are also picking up nothing.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.890
It's no good; there's no response whatsoever from any of them.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.880
Let's try switching over to 3D measurement.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.820
Once again, nothing...

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:27.980
Not even horizontally?

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.150
No, nothing.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:35.200
That's crazy. This cavern isn't more than ten meters across!

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.360
And still we can't measure it?!

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.800
But there's a faint sound, isn't there?

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.940
440 Hz... It's the tone of A.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.340
I wonder if this isn't connected to another space?

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.940
So are you saying that this cavern is the source of the Dynamis?

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.140
Yes...

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.180
We've finished deciphering the inscriptions.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:01.080
This entire ruin seems to be the tomb of Gilgamesh.

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.020
Gilgamesh?!

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.560
Apparently, a mummy rests beneath the stone monument.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:11.760
Then the entire tomb was serving to seal off this cavern.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.670
That could be.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:16.500
This is a tremendous discovery!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.110
Gilgamesh and Enkidu...

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:35.790
In days to follow, Gilgamesh's mummy was also discovered in the altar which had been sealing off this cavern.

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:40.220
It's said that Gilgamesh was part human and part god.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:43.130
If so, then naturally it stands to reason,

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:46.000
...that the genetic material of the gods has been passed on to that mummy as well.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:49.540
<i>The cavern was named Delphys, "the womb of the gods,"</i>

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:53.900
<i>...and this entire vicinity was designated as a zone under the joint control of the international community.</i>

00:13:53.980 --> 00:14:00.080
It signifies that it's been recognized that this discovery is one of great value to humankind.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:07.390
It means it was judged that this ought not to be owned by any single individual, or any existing group or nation.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:12.350
<i>And so leading scientists are to be gathered from all nations at this spot,</i>

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.790
<i>...and an enormous research institution is to be established.</i>

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:18.600
<i>Its name will be Heaven's Gate.</i>

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.260
<i>The Delphys subspace and the gods' genetic material...</i>

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:23.140
<i>The elucidation of these findings will be their mission.</i>

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:27.470
So everything is going over to Heaven's Gate then.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:33.150
We've got nothing more to do here. We've decided we'll pull out soon.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.610
It was really fun, being able to meet you.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.050
The pleasure was mine. Sorry to put you through so much trouble.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.620
I hear you're going to participate at Heaven's Gate.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:47.560
It's a nest of academism, the thing you detest most.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:49.630
You'll likely have lots of enemies.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.100
That's another reason why I feel I have an obligation to stay.

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.500
In order to keep them from just doing as they like.

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:59.630
The rumor is that the main sponsor is Japanese.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.200
His name, as I recall, is Yuki.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:03.910
Yuki?

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.850
I wonder if you know him?

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.410
A bit, from before...

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:10.810
Seems like he's not very well spoken of, huh?

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.220
So it's under the auspices of that old man?

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.750
Then I can afford to take my eyes off of it even less.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.400
Everything's coming along well.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:21.690
That's good.

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.730
To think that Terumichi's going to be a papa...

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.200
Do you intend to have it here?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.140
Terumichi told me to have it in Japan.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:38.040
He said we can't have Dynamis harming the child in my womb.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.070
What's the matter?

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:47.150
It just seems like, while I'm back home, Terumichi will up and vanish and be gone.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.860
Why would you say such a thing?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.660
It's because he's just too caring.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:59.730
I've never had a caring guy like that up till now.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:05.170
That boy has also come through hard times since he was little.

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:08.370
That's why he was able to become so caring.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.450
That's something we know too.

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:15.080
Terumichi would never do anything to make you unhappy.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:17.710
Right? So set your mind at rest.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.820
You're going to be a mother soon, right?

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:24.860
The child inside you will become unhappy too, so no more crying.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.290
Okay...

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.460
Have you decided on a name yet?

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.290
Kiyoko...

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:35.440
I swear I'll cherish Kiyoko.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:42.900
The fetus is growing?

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:44.710
Yes...

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:47.010
That can't be...

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:50.290
So you're still trying to give me trouble.

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:54.730
What shall we do, my lady?

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:56.590
Do you even need to ask?

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:58.030
What are you planning to do?

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:00.420
Begin immediately, please.

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:05.060
Don't!

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:08.600
Don't hurt my big sister any more than you already have!

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.840
I can't believe what you're saying.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.510
Your sister is already dead.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.450
On top of that, the child inside her...

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:17.950
Shut up! Shut your mouth!

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:21.350
A child of Gilgamesh mustn't be born into this world.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.750
What calamities it might bring for humanity...

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:26.720
Shut up, shut up! Shut your mouth, you old hag!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.820
I wish we'd never had anything to do with you!

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:32.090
Then my sister wouldn't have ended up like this!

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:34.260
That's not true.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.160
I said, shut up!

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:38.840
Stop it!

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.100
If it weren't for you...

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.030
Is everything all right, my lady?

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.210
Yes...

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.430
How about taking a bit of a rest, my lady?

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:20.770
I shall prepare some tea.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.380
Yes, please.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:24.640
As you wish, my lady.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.880
<i>Shut up, shut up! Shut your mouth, you old hag!</i>

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.620
<i>If it weren't for you...</i>

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.150
<i>I wonder what it was that changed you?</i>

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:37.990
<i>You looked so happy when you were a girl.</i>

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.730
<i>Hey, shall I take a picture for you?</i>

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.610
<i>You look prettiest when you smile.</i>

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:10.580
I did the job you told me to. I'm gonna hold you to your promise.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.860
I know.

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:19.370
Well, life is full of surprises. Don't head down the wrong path.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.970
I guess that's not persuasive coming from me.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.750
Takaaki Kagami...

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.480
Haruka Mayuzumi...

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.380
Shouichi Kidokoro...

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:44.090
How we were born is in these papers.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.600
Master Toru, is something the matter?

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:06.470
My mother gave birth to me... my mother...

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:25.100
Is it only you?

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:26.930
Yes...

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:29.500
What's the matter with the other two?

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:34.140
They seem to be indisposed. In their place, I've brought guests.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.030
You're acquainted with them, aren't you?

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.120
Yes...

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:56.200
Tonight, at long last, won't you tell me?

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:59.070
About what happened at Heaven's Gate,

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.070
...and for what purpose you gathered us here?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:15.480
I am not you!

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:29.950
I already know that we were born from the cloned embryos from Orga which were contaminated by Tear.

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:31.790
And how we were born, as well.

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:34.260
Why did you search us out?

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:36.060
Why didn't you just leave us alone?

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:40.160
I've never been able to forget the day I first met you either.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:42.330
I could hardly believe someone so beautiful existed.

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:45.540
She said when she saw you for the first time, it was just like she was dreaming.

00:23:45.540 --> 00:23:48.370
All of us ended up living together in this hotel.

00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:49.610
It was foolish, wasn't it?

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:54.070
Thinking I might even be able to die for your sake...
